Warning: Spoilers ahead for "Game of Thrones" season seven.
The latest "Game of Thrones" episode concluded with two major castle battles (and an epic mic-drop death scene from Olenna Tyrell). But even though seeing the Lannister and Unsullied armies in full regalia was pretty badass, some people were severely underwhelmed at the sight of the two castles: Casterly Rock and Highgarden.
Ahead of the episode, fans knew Casterly Rock would make an appearance. Everyone was getting hyped up on Twitter and Reddit.
Unsullied will try to capture Casterly Rock next week. Considered impregnable by even Visenya Targaryen, it is 3 times the size of the Wall pic.twitter.com/IxNwFM93A5 — Al Swearengen (@RealPeterman) July 24, 2017
I can't believe we're finally going to see Casterly Rock. This is something I've always dreamed of. #GameofThrones pic.twitter.com/Yf9KrTQ9Ee — Lady Lauren �� (@speedyphoebe) July 29, 2017
Whole Reddit threads were dedicated to how excited book readers were to finally see the Lannister stronghold on their TV screens. But then the mountain we were expecting wound up being much smaller.
Book readers had a similar reaction to Highgarden. People thought the Tyrell castle didn't appear nearly as lush and rich as they'd imagined. Some even got confused, and thought it was just the other side of Casterly Rock — not a different castle entirely.
when u order it online vs when it arrives pic.twitter.com/4UbANZuzK4 — jess (@cerseisreign) July 31, 2017
